<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The Cua Driver helper (Contents/Helpers/cua-driver). Every entitlement
	     here must carry evidence that this process needs it; today there is
	     none.

	     The shell starts the driver in embedded mode, which never disclaims
	     responsibility: Avibe.app stays the responsible process, so macOS
	     attributes Accessibility, Screen Recording, and any Automation consent
	     to the app's code identity, not to this helper's entitlements.

	     Deliberately absent: com.apple.security.automation.apple-events and
	     com.apple.security.device.screen-capture, which upstream signs its
	     standalone driver with. Screen capture has no hardened-runtime
	     entitlement; TCC alone grants it. launch_app attaches an oapp Apple
	     Event to an NSWorkspace launch, and a hardened process with no
	     entitlements, even as its own responsible process, launches an app
	     with that event attached. AppleScript that set_value runs goes
	     through a separate /usr/bin/osascript process. -->
</dict>
</plist>
